# Build context for `analysis/eventhound.Dockerfile` — the one image built from the repository root.
#
# ALLOWLIST, deliberately. The root of this repository holds `data/` — real client material, §10 —
# and multi-gigabyte local caches (venvs, .tools, case databases), none of which an image built
# from here has any business seeing.
#
# DO NOT re-include a parent directory to "help the walker descend". That was the first version of
# this file and it silently defeated the allowlist: Docker's matcher re-tests every pattern against
# each PARENT PREFIX of a path (`MatchesOrParentMatches` in moby/patternmatcher — the same rule that
# makes a bare `node_modules` exclude everything under it), and it applies that rule to `!` patterns
# too. BuildKit descends into `analysis/` and `tools/` on its own, because the exceptions below are
# prefixed by them.
#
# NOTE for whoever adds the next root-context image: this file is why your build sees nothing.
# Add your paths to the allowlist rather than deleting it.
**

# --- eventhound.Dockerfile ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The engine and the GUI, plus the shared `tools/` the whole tree imports through sys.path.
!analysis
!analysis/**

# --- shared tools --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only the modules `analysis/` actually imports: eventhound_config (settings + API keys), scoring
# (the deterministic oracle, §6) and enrichment.
!tools/eventhound_config.py
!tools/scoring
!tools/scoring/**
!tools/enrichment
!tools/enrichment/**

# --- re-excluded, whatever the rules above re-included ---------------------------------------
# `analysis/.tools/` holds the HOST's macOS Hayabusa and EZ-tool binaries, and the image downloads
# the Linux ones into the same path at build time.
analysis/.tools
analysis/.tools/**
analysis/reports
analysis/reports/**
analysis/yara_rules
analysis/yara_rules/**
analysis/sigma/community
analysis/sigma/community/**
**/.venv
**/.venv/**
**/logs
**/logs/**
**/tests
**/tests/**
**/*.evtx
**/*.pcap
**/*.pcapng
**/*.duckdb
**/__pycache__
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
